  "notes": "{吹|ふ}く describes blowing air or wind movement. It can be intransitive (wind blows) or transitive (to blow something).\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Intransitive: ⟦{風|かぜ}→風：00641_kaze⟧⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧{吹|ふ}く (wind blows)\n- Transitive: ⟦{笛|ふえ}→笛：03593_fue⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{吹|ふ}く (to play a flute)\n\nASPECT (ている):\n⟦{風|かぜ}→風：00641_kaze⟧⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧{吹|ふ}いて⟦いる→いる：00495_iru⟧ means the wind is currently blowing (ongoing action).\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- ⟦{風|かぜ}→風：00641_kaze⟧⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧{吹|ふ}く: wind blows\n- ⟦{笛|ふえ}→笛：03593_fue⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{吹|ふ}く: to play the flute\n- ⟦ラッパ→ラッパ：09958_rappa⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{吹|ふ}く: to play the trumpet\n- ⟦{息|いき}→息：02176_iki⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{吹|ふ}き⟦かける→かける：00854_kakeru⟧: to blow breath on\n- ⟦シャボン{玉|だま}→シャボン玉：27863_shabondama⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{吹|ふ}く: to blow bubbles\n\nNOTE: For wind instruments, {吹|ふ}く is the standard verb for \"to play.\"",
